CodeForge — LICENSE (PENDING — NOT YET AN OPERATIVE GRANT)
============================================================

STATUS: OWNER_AUTHORIZATION_REQUIRED

This file is NOT a LICENSE. It is not currently referenced by the "License: MIT" badge in
README.md, and its text below has no legal effect until a project owner explicitly authorizes it
and it is renamed to `LICENSE`.

Why this file exists instead of a real LICENSE
------------------------------------------------
The MIT license *type* is already declared clearly and consistently in three independent places
in this repository:

  - package.json:               "license": "MIT"
  - README.md:                  License badge + "## License / MIT" section
  - CONTRIBUTING.md:             "CodeForge is MIT licensed. Contributions welcome."

That is sufficient evidence to formalize the MIT license text — but the COPYRIGHT HOLDER named in
an MIT grant is a separate fact, and it is NOT yet settled. Pass-3's business-decisions register
(docs/legal/pass3/final-business-decisions.md, BIZ-01) records "Forger Digital Solutions" only as
a RECOMMENDED name pending explicit project-owner approval — not a confirmed legal entity. Issuing
a copyright grant on behalf of an entity whose legal status (registered company? sole
proprietorship DBA? unregistered project name?) is unconfirmed would be exactly the kind of
"legally operative grant on behalf of an uncertain entity" the R1 legal remediation spec (§4)
says engineering must not do unilaterally.

What happens next
------------------
Once the project owner confirms the copyright holder name to use (see BIZ-01 in
docs/legal/pass3/final-business-decisions.md and the disposition entry for LEG-P0-01 in
docs/legal/remediation/r1-issue-disposition.md):

  1. Replace "[OWNER_AUTHORIZATION_REQUIRED]" below with the confirmed name.
  2. Rename this file to `LICENSE` (git mv LICENSE.pending LICENSE).
  3. Remove this header block above the "MIT License" heading.

The MIT terms below are the standard, unmodified MIT License text and are not themselves in
question — only the copyright line is pending.

